{"seq":1253,"lane":"judging","class":"lower-bound-treated-as-point","severity":"serious","evidence":"1253.json, v83: “The guidance supports revenue above $40 billion, but does not quantify growth beyond doubling enough to imply at least $45 billion.” The judgement selects the $40 billion to below $45 billion outcome.","rule":"Standard §5.4 requires preserving a statement’s limits; §7 and D218 require the judgement to distinguish evidence from inference.","mechanism":"The source says revenue will more than double, which leaves the upper end open. The judgement treats that lower bound as sufficient to select a bounded outcome."}
{"seq":1253,"lane":"matching","class":"same-article-evidence-duplicated","severity":"serious","evidence":"1253.json: “Kress said Nvidia not only still expects $20 billion in CPU revenue in its fiscal 2027, but expects that number to more than double in fiscal 2028.” The ledger stores this statement as e4368 under v83 and e4373 under v7.","rule":"Standard §2 and D250: one research matter in one article is one record; a record can link to relevant questions.","mechanism":"A and B independently return overlapping passages, and the handover writes both as separate evidence records."}
{"seq":1253,"lane":"matching","class":"same-article-evidence-duplicated","severity":"serious","evidence":"1253.json: “Now, his new estimate is $210 billion, due to the rise of AI agents.” The ledger stores the same server CPU market estimate as e4370 under v83 and e4374 under v7.","rule":"Standard §2 and D250: one research matter in one article is one record; a record can link to relevant questions.","mechanism":"A and B independently return the same passage, and the handover writes both records."}
{"seq":1253,"lane":"A","class":"background-kept-as-evidence","severity":"minor","evidence":"1253.json, A e2: “If the market keeps growing, there should be plenty of room for AMD and Intel to get their piece of the pie.”","rule":"Standard §5.3 excludes general background and a named analyst’s interpretation without a new fact or calculation.","mechanism":"A retains a generic conditional interpretation as evidence for v83; its passage review does not remove it."}
{"seq":1253,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"unsupported-statement-time","severity":"minor","evidence":"1253.json, A e1: “expects that number to more than double in fiscal 2028”; record preparation sets event_time to “Kress said last quarter; the report gives no exact day.” The article applies “last quarter” to the earlier FY2027 projection.","rule":"Standard §2 and §5.4 require the original timing and the limits of a statement to be preserved.","mechanism":"Record preparation appears to transfer the timing of the earlier FY2027 projection to the combined statement that also contains the FY2028 expectation."}
{"seq":1253,"lane":"matching","class":"invented-statement-date","severity":"serious","evidence":"1253.json, handover e7 has original_day “”; matching supplies said_day “2026-08-30” and returns “replace” for the server CPU market estimate.","rule":"D203 requires an unknown original statement day to remain unknown; D202 distinguishes a later revision from a repeat or different statement.","mechanism":"src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:265 substitutes the article publication day when original_day is empty, so the comparison receives a date the source did not establish. The trace alone does not establish whether the replacement verdict would change without it."}
{"seq":1254,"lane":"A","class":"background-kept-as-evidence","severity":"minor","evidence":"1254.json, A e3: “An AI cloud is an emerging kind of intermediary, one that buys Nvidia's chips, packs them into clusters, and leases capacity to companies that never need to negotiate with a chip designer directly.”","rule":"Standard §5.3 excludes general background and descriptions of existing arrangements without a new action.","mechanism":"A retains an explanation of a business model as evidence for v84."}
{"seq":1254,"lane":"A","class":"background-kept-as-evidence","severity":"minor","evidence":"1254.json, A e4: “Manufacturers running digital twins on the factory floor, a bank assessing risk , or a government designing a sovereign cluster is far more complex than a corporation simply increasing its operating budget to rent incremental storage on AWS.”","rule":"Standard §5.3 excludes general background without a new fact or concrete development.","mechanism":"A retains illustrative customer descriptions as evidence for v84, although the passage does not report a new customer action or figure."}
{"seq":1254,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"wrong-original-attribution","severity":"serious","evidence":"1254.json, A e1 reports the quarterly company figures; record preparation assigns “original_who”: “Adam Spatacco”, “original_day”: “2026-08-30”, and “tier”: “fact”.","rule":"Standard §2 and §5.4 require the original speaker and date; an unknown original date stays unknown.","mechanism":"Record preparation attributes figures reported from NVIDIA’s earnings to the article author and uses the article date as their original date."}
{"seq":1254,"lane":"matching","class":"same-article-evidence-duplicated","severity":"serious","evidence":"1254.json: “The AI Clouds, Industrial, and Enterprise group (ACIE) generated $40.3 billion, an increase of 25% from last quarter and 138% year over year.” The ledger stores it in e4375 under v84 and e4381 under v10.","rule":"Standard §2 and D250: one research matter in one article is one record; a record can link to relevant questions.","mechanism":"A includes the customer-group figures in its opening passage and B returns the ACIE figure separately; both survive as records with different original attribution."}
{"seq":1254,"lane":"matching","class":"same-article-evidence-duplicated","severity":"serious","evidence":"1254.json: “Hyperscale customers generated $48.7 billion in revenue, up 13% sequentially and 102% from a year ago.” The ledger stores it in e4375 under v84 and e4380 under v10.","rule":"Standard §2 and D250: one research matter in one article is one record; a record can link to relevant questions.","mechanism":"A’s combined passage and B’s separate hyperscaler passage both survive as records."}
{"seq":1254,"lane":"judging","class":"past-growth-extrapolated","severity":"serious","evidence":"1254.json, v84: “Carrying the reported 25% sequential growth forward gives an implied FY2027 total of about $185.9 billion, above rung 1's $177.32 billion boundary.”","rule":"Standard §7 and D218 require the judgement to distinguish source evidence from inference and explain the support for its conclusion; D260 asks for the outcome the evidence makes most likely.","mechanism":"The judgement repeats one observed quarter’s growth rate for both remaining quarters and selects the strongest outcome. The cited passages give no forecast that this rate will persist; judging-v7 asks the model to carry guided growth forward, but this growth was observed rather than guided."}
{"seq":1255,"lane":"B","class":"missing-supply-evidence","severity":"serious","evidence":"1255.json: “The company is partnering with NVIDIA to build three advanced optical-manufacturing facilities in North Carolina and Texas. The project is expected to create more than 3,000 jobs and expand Corning’s U.S. optical-manufacturing capacity tenfold.” B returns no evidence.","rule":"Standard §5.1 keeps a concrete named-party plan an analyst would note; D259 permits evidence bearing on supply behind an existing question.","mechanism":"B does not connect the NVIDIA-linked optical capacity plan to an existing data-center or networking question. The trace does not establish why it omitted the passage."}
{"seq":1256,"lane":"B","class":"quote-summary-mismatch","severity":"minor","evidence":"1256.json, e1 quotes “Nvidia (NasdaqGS: NVDA) agreed to acquire AI platform Hugging Face for US$12.9b in a cash and stock deal announced on 27 August 2026.” Its one_line adds “remains subject to regulatory approvals.”","rule":"Standard §2 requires a verbatim passage and a standalone summary of the recorded statement with accurate sourcing.","mechanism":"B combines the deal announcement and an approval condition from a separate article sentence into a summary whose retained quote contains only the first."}
{"seq":1257,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-evidence-home","severity":"serious","evidence":"1257.json: “During TSMC's last quarterly conference call, CEO C.C. Wei told investors that he expects elevated chip demand to last through at least 2029 or 2030.” B links it to v2, NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue; v79 already asks for TSMC fiscal 2026 total revenue.","rule":"D207 and D259 require helpful evidence to go to the narrowest existing question it bears on.","mechanism":"B uses NVIDIA’s broad revenue question for a foundry CEO’s demand outlook without selecting the existing question about that foundry’s own revenue."}
{"seq":1258,"lane":"B","class":"multiple-existing-homes","severity":"serious","evidence":"1258.json: “The companies also plan to bring new Vera-based CPUs into Amazon's cloud to support increasingly advanced AI applications.” The ledger links e4387 to v7, v24 and v83.","rule":"D207, D259 and D360 specify one narrowest existing home for daily filing, with the same answer’s new candidates as a separate allowance.","mechanism":"B returns three existing-question links for one undated deployment plan, and build_handover preserves all of them."}
{"seq":1258,"lane":"B","class":"multiple-existing-homes","severity":"serious","evidence":"1258.json: “Nvidia and AWS have built one of the great growth engines of the AI era, and demand is running ahead of every forecast.” The ledger links e4389 to v2, v4, v5 and v10.","rule":"D207, D259 and D360 specify one narrowest existing home for daily filing.","mechanism":"B returns four existing-question links, including both broad company revenue and narrower questions, and build_handover preserves them."}
{"seq":1259,"lane":"drop","class":"helpful-evidence-dropped","severity":"serious","evidence":"1259.json: “SWI Group … has announced that it has become a member of the NVIDIA Cloud Partner (NCP) program as a Preferred Partner.” The article also says it plans to deploy NVIDIA GPUs in its AI factories. Handover drops the passages as “no existing question linked”.","rule":"Standard §5.1 and D240 keep relevant named-party actions even without an amount; D209 requires missed helpful drops to be identified.","mechanism":"B produces passages but gives them no existing-question link, so the handover drops the new partner action and its stated deployment plan instead of filing the demand evidence."}
{"seq":1260,"lane":"B","class":"unhelpful-revenue-share-link","severity":"minor","evidence":"1260.json: “As of June 30, the company held $63.44 billion in public stock across eight positions as shown below.” B links it to v81, “What share of NVIDIA’s FY2028 revenue will come from customers it has financed in some way?”","rule":"Standard §5.1 and D259 require a statement to bear on the linked question through an identifiable path.","mechanism":"B treats the total value of a mixed investment portfolio as evidence for a future share of revenue from financed customers. The total does not identify customer financing or the revenue share."}
{"summary":{"items_read":[1253,1254,1255,1256,1257,1258,1259,1260],"classes":{"lower-bound-treated-as-point":1,"same-article-evidence-duplicated":4,"background-kept-as-evidence":3,"unsupported-statement-time":1,"invented-statement-date":1,"wrong-original-attribution":1,"past-growth-extrapolated":1,"missing-supply-evidence":1,"quote-summary-mismatch":1,"wrong-evidence-home":1,"multiple-existing-homes":2,"helpful-evidence-dropped":1,"unhelpful-revenue-share-link":1}}}